// PINS: two field names that differ only in `-` vs `_` collide in the
// emitted struct — kebab mangles to snake at identifier formation on every
// target, so `a-b` and `a_b` write one member downstream and the field
// list must refuse the pair at declaration.
const std = @import("std");
~tor scan {}
| found { a-b: i32, a_b: i64 }
| miss
~scan => miss
~scan()
| found f |> _
| miss |> _
